<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reginar, Duke of Lorraine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 850–915</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Reginar Longneck</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reginar Longneck was the leading noble of Lotharingia at the end of the 9th century. He held counties around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scheldt">Scheldt</a>, including Hainaut, and lay abbacies such as Echternach, and was recognised as duke or margrave in Lotharingia. His descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reginarids">Reginarids</a>, became counts of Hainaut and later dukes of Brabant.</p></div>
